.TH FOMKYR 1 "October 2026" "fomkyr 0.6.8"
.SH NAME
fomkyr \- fast pure C engine for exact homogeneous noncommutative Groebner bases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fomkyr
.BI \-i " input.bg"
.BI \-d " degree"
.BI \-j " workers"
.BI \-\-workdir " directory"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B fomkyr
.BI \-\-resume " directory"
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A standalone C engine with pthread workers and durable checkpoints. George's
optional WebAssembly backend uses the same direct-exact kernel. Expanded homogeneous polynomial inputs and exact JSON
fixtures are supported. The field is Q unless a prime characteristic is given.
The last declared generator is greatest in degree-left-lex order.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-memory " auto|SIZE"
One allocation ceiling. K, M, G and T are binary units. Native execution has no
WASM application ceiling; OS and representation limits still apply.
.TP
.B \-\-wasm
Execute the packaged WebAssembly engine using Node, retaining WASM memory limits.
.TP
.B \-\-wasm-limit
Keep native execution but impose the WASM application memory ceiling.
.TP
.BI \-\-checkpoint-seconds " N"
Checkpoint interval at quiescent frontiers; default 30. Not a bound on lost
uncommitted work. Zero requests a save at every available frontier.
.TP
.BI \-\-time-limit " N"
Request cancellation after N seconds. Exit code 124 indicates deadline interruption.
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the newest valid matching checkpoint without computing or changing job files.
.TP
.B \-\-fresh
Explicitly discard the matching algebra's existing cache. Not a corruption-repair mode.
.TP
.B \-\-hilbert
Export completed-degree Hilbert coefficients.
.TP
.B \-\-export
Stream result.gb after completion.
.TP
.B \-\-human
Print readable terminal progress and summaries, with elapsed time in seconds.
Supported by native and optional Wasm CLI modes. JSON is the default; persisted
metadata and the explicit --dump-fixture output remain JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress progress and checkpoint messages; retain the final summary.
.TP
.BI \-\-hilbert-certificate " FILE"
Replay exact independent integer-dual lower bounds and enable equality-based
degree closure. Off by default. Requires a matching input/order/field.
.TP
.BI \-\-assume-hilbert " FILE"
Explicitly trust external dimension statements. Output and checkpoints are
labelled conditional on this document. This is not a replayable certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-hilbert-fixed-batch
Disable bound-aware batch lookahead in the optional closure mode.
.TP
.B \-\-fk-gate
Explicitly accept the compiled FK Gate 0.3 product-permutation dimension profile.
Only the authenticated original-order FK6 presentation over Q, through degree 17,
is eligible. Output is conditional on the imported dimensions; the referenced
proof bundle is not replayed by the runtime. Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-fk-total-only
Use the same imported authority for total-degree closure without sector skips.
.TP
.BI \-\-fk-gate-memory " SIZE"
Maximum temporary space for the optional normal-word counter (default 128M).
This is separate from, and remains within, the overall memory ceiling.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGUSR1 requests a safe checkpoint and continues. SIGINT and SIGTERM request
cancellation and retain a safe frontier. SIGKILL cannot create a new checkpoint.
Committed pairs are retained; uncommitted reductions are replayed on resume.
For a resumable break, press Ctrl+C, wait for exit, then restart with
--resume DIR and the desired degree bound.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: requested task complete; 2: invalid input/command; 65: rejected lower-bound witness;
66: status found no checkpoint;
70: runtime failure; 75: memory/workspace resource failure; 124: deadline;
128+signal: handled interruption.
.SH FILES
The job directory contains fixture.json, job.json, cli.lock and a content-keyed
fomkyr/alg-* directory. Basis records have ABI 3; mid-degree frontiers use version 1.
Scalar-Hilbert metadata uses ABI 4. FK-Gate metadata uses ABI 5 and requires
the same imported profile on resume; prior scalar authorities are retained. Do not
open FK-Gate jobs with 0.6.7 or older: old readers may ignore this metadata
and fall back to earlier checkpoints. Ordinary records retain ABI 3.
.SH LIMITATIONS
No guarantee of termination, available physical memory, or bounded cancellation
latency. Active polynomial state is not serialized. Linux/x86-64 GCC/Clang execution
was tested; native records require a little-endian host in this release.
.SH SEE ALSO
The distributed README.md and docs/HILBERT_CLOSURE.md.

.SH SCHEDULING
The default cooperative scheduler preserves unfinished exact reductions across
soft time slices and commits ready rows after exact updated-basis reduction.
.TP
.B --scheduler cooperative|barrier
Choose cooperative scheduling (default) or whole-batch barrier scheduling.
.TP
.B --quantum-ms N
Soft worker slice target, 1 to 10000 milliseconds; default 250.
.TP
.B --big-row-max-terms N
Ceiling for the sparse arbitrary-precision rational table. Default auto (also
0) derives capacity from the row workspace. An explicit ceiling must be a
power of two from 128 to 1073741824; 1048576 restores a one-million-slot cap.
Growth and reserve promotion retain the unfinished exact reduction. The memory
allowance remains binding. This affects table slots, not the final basis size.
.TP
.B --cache-percent N
Worker record cache as a percentage of each lane workspace, 0 to 40; default 12.
A smaller cache leaves more room for exact row reduction. This can help when
the shared immutable cache already holds the frequently used reducers.
.TP
.B --shared-cache SIZE
Pinned immutable reducer records, in binary K/M/G/T units. Default auto uses
one sixteenth of the memory allowance; 0 disables pinning. This allocation
remains inside the total budget.
.TP
.B --lookahead N
Initial pending pair window, 1 to 512; default 128.
.TP
.B --max-lookahead N
Ceiling for elastic window growth, 1 to 512; default 512. While elasticity is
enabled, this must be at least the initial lookahead. Growth supplies idle lanes
with additional work when long reductions occupy the current window.
.TP
.B --no-elastic-window
Keep the pending window fixed at the initial lookahead.
.TP
.B --no-sector-priority
Disable FK Gate component-deficit ordering of substantial input rows. The
default prioritizes nearly closed components, then smaller estimated input rows,
when component dimensions and cost scheduling are active.
.TP
.B --no-radix-cache
Disable cached exact bucket maxima.
.TP
.B --no-helper-rows
Disable bounded helper calculations while primary rows wait for the shared
exceptional reserve. Helpers are enabled by default when their independent
arenas fit within the memory budget. Unfinished primary rows retain their state.
